# Magnetic CIF (CIF 1.1 syntax)
data_KCuF3_bulk_G_AFM
# Fully expanded conventional cell: all 20 atoms explicitly listed.
# Identity-only (P1 subgroup) encoding; maximal magnetic symmetry is not assigned.
# Nuclear structure: bulk a-polytype, I4/mcm (No. 140), standard setting.
# The structural polytype name a is distinct from magnetic A-type ordering.
# Model magnetic moments are +/-1 mu_B along the conventional a axis.
# Geometry is fixed for both magnetic models; no magnetic-state relaxation.

_chemical_name_common 'Bulk KCuF3 G-type AFM model'
_chemical_formula_sum 'K Cu F3'
_cell_formula_units_Z 4
_cell_length_a 5.856900
_cell_length_b 5.856900
_cell_length_c 7.848700
_cell_angle_alpha 90
_cell_angle_beta 90
_cell_angle_gamma 90
_cell_volume 269.236135

_publ_section_comment
;
Antiparallel Cu moments on every nearest-neighbor Cu-Cu bond, in plane and along c.
Bulk JT-distorted I4/mcm a-polytype geometry with a=b=5.8569 Angstrom,
c=7.8487 Angstrom, and equatorial F 8h coordinate x=0.22803.
These structural parameters are reported by Towler, Dovesi and Saunders,
Phys. Rev. B 52, 10150-10159 (1995), DOI 10.1103/PhysRevB.52.10150.
Parent Wyckoff sites: K 4a (0,0,1/4); Cu 4d (0,1/2,0);
apical F 4b (0,1/2,1/4); equatorial F 8h (x,x+1/2,0).
The conventional cell contains two Cu planes at z=0 and z=1/2.
Magnetic moments are normalized model values, not a measured refinement.
The common spin axis is [100] in the conventional tetragonal cell.
K and F moments are set to zero. The net cell magnetic moment is zero.
G-type is an imposed comparison configuration, not asserted to be the ambient bulk ground state.
All atoms and moments are expanded explicitly using an identity-only
magnetic symmetry subgroup. No claim of maximal P1 symmetry is made.
;

